# <type>(<optional scope>): <short description>
#
# Types: feat, fix, docs, refactor, test, chore
# Scopes: http, service, repository, domain, config, db (optional)
# Use imperative wording, keep the subject within 72 characters,
# and omit the trailing period.
# Example: feat(http): add filtering by due date

# Explain why the change was made, if needed. Separate the body
# from the subject with a blank line.

# For breaking changes, add ! before the subject's colon and a footer:
# BREAKING CHANGE: Describe the change and required migration.
